{%- comment -%}
  HIVOLT — templates/page.track-order.liquid
  ──────────────────────────────────────────
  Alternate page template. In the admin: Pages → Track Your Order → Template
  suffix → "track-order". Renders inside layout/theme.liquid, which supplies
  <main>.

  Styles live in site/theme/pages.css. build-theme.py concatenates that into
  the single assets/hivolt.css that layout/theme.liquid already links, after
  theme-hivolt.css — so there is no second stylesheet to add.

  There is no tracking-number lookup box on this page, and that is deliberate.

  A form here could only take a number and hand it to a carrier — it cannot
  read the order, because Shopify does not expose order lookup by number to a
  logged-out storefront. A box that pretends to search and then redirects is a
  worse experience than the two routes that genuinely work:

    · signed in  → the real order list, rendered below from customer.orders,
                   each row linking to its own live status page
    · signed out → the status link in the confirmation email, which is
                   authenticated by the token in it

  So the page shows whichever of those two applies, and says plainly why there
  is nothing to type into.
{%- endcomment -%}

<nav class="crumb wrap" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
  <ol>
    <li><a href="{{ routes.root_url }}">Home</a></li>
    <li aria-current="page">{{ page.title | default: 'Track your order' | escape }}</li>
  </ol>
</nav>

<section class="hero hero--doc wrap">
  <p class="mono hero__eyebrow">Order status</p>
  <h1 class="hero__h">Two ways<br>to find<br><em>your order.</em></h1>
  <p class="hero__sub">
    {%- if customer -%}
      You're signed in, so your orders are listed below with their live status.
    {%- else -%}
      Sign in for the full list, or use the status link in your confirmation
      email — it works without an account.
    {%- endif -%}
  </p>
</section>

<section class="pg wrap">
  <div class="pg__cols">

    <div class="rte">
      {%- if page.content != blank -%}
        {{ page.content }}
      {%- else -%}
        <p>
          Every order ships with tracking. The status page updates as the order
          is made, dispatched and scanned by the carrier.
        </p>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>

    <aside class="pg__aside">

      {%- if customer -%}
        <p class="mono pg__aside-h">Your orders</p>

        {%- if customer.orders.size > 0 -%}
          <div class="sheet">
            {%- for order in customer.orders limit: 8 -%}
              <div class="sheet__row">
                <span class="sheet__k">
                  <a href="{{ order.customer_url }}">{{ order.name }}</a>
                </span>
                <span class="sheet__v">
                  <em>{{ order.fulfillment_status_label | default: 'Not fulfilled' }}</em>
                </span>
              </div>
              <div class="sheet__row">
                <span class="sheet__k">Placed</span>
                <span class="sheet__v">{{ order.created_at | date: '%d %b %Y' }}</span>
              </div>
            {%- endfor -%}
          </div>
          <p class="sheet__src">
            Each order number links to its own live status page. Statuses come
            from the carrier and can lag a scan by a few hours.
          </p>
          {%- if customer.orders_count > 8 -%}
            <div class="rte rte--tight" style="margin-top:14px">
              <p><a href="{{ routes.account_url }}">See all {{ customer.orders_count }} orders</a></p>
            </div>
          {%- endif -%}

        {%- else -%}
          <div class="rte rte--tight">
            <p>
              There are no orders on this account yet. When you place one, it
              appears here with its status.
            </p>
            <p><a href="{{ routes.all_products_collection_url }}">Browse the catalogue</a></p>
          </div>
        {%- endif -%}

      {%- else -%}
        <p class="mono pg__aside-h">Signed out</p>
        <div class="rte rte--tight">
          <p>
            <strong>From the confirmation email.</strong> The order confirmation
            carries a status link unique to that order. It opens the live status
            page without an account and without a password.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>From an account.</strong> Signing in lists every order placed
            with the same email address, each with its own status.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="rte rte--tight" style="margin-top:18px">
          <p><a href="{{ routes.account_login_url }}">Sign in</a> &nbsp;·&nbsp; <a href="{{ routes.account_register_url }}">Create an account</a></p>
        </div>
      {%- endif -%}

      <p class="mono pg__aside-h pg__aside-h--gap">Can't find the email?</p>
      <div class="rte rte--tight">
        <p>
          Check the spam folder first, then write in with the email address used
          at checkout. That is enough to locate the order.
        </p>
      </div>
    </aside>

  </div>
</section>

<section class="pg__qw wrap">
  <div class="pg__q">
    <p class="pg__q-t">
      <span class="mono">Tracking hasn't moved?</span>
      A label can be created a day or two before the carrier scans it, so a
      stationary number early on is normal. If it hasn't moved after that, write
      in with the order number.
    </p>
    {%- assign contact_page = pages['contact-us'] | default: pages['contact'] -%}
    <a class="btn" href="{{ contact_page.url | default: '/pages/contact-us' }}">Ask about an order</a>
  </div>
</section>
